e6_cyclic_sharp.py  seed=20261012

(a) component laws by exhaustive enumeration of their randomness (exact rationals)
   n=2: 6 orderings, 252 exact comparisons with the closed forms, mismatches: 0
   n=3: 4 orderings, 840 exact comparisons with the closed forms, mismatches: 0
   closed forms: cyclic 1/(N-1)_k; broom B_j: 1/(N-1)_{k-1} if j=k, 1/(N-1)_k if j>k, 0 if j<k (k>=2);
   partial chain P_j: 1/(N-1)_k if j>=k; normaliser of P_j at x_t: (j-t+1)/((N-t)(N-1)_{t-1}) for j>=t.
   example n=3, k=4: broom B_4 gives 1/210, cyclic law 1/840

(b) depth-count lemma |A_k(F)| <= N - k
   n=2: all 625 partial functions; max |A_k| for k=1..3: [3, 2, 1]; bound N-k: [3, 2, 1]
   n=3: all 8^8 = 16777216 total functions; max |A_k| for k=1..7: [7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1]; bound N-k: [7, 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1]; violations: 0  (11 s)
   n=3: 100000 random partial functions (values uniform on undefined/0..N-1); max |A_k|, k=1..7: [6, 5, 4, 4, 3, 2, 1]; violations: 0
   n=4: 100000 random partial functions (values uniform on undefined/0..N-1); max |A_k|, k=1..15: [7, 9, 8, 8, 6, 6, 6, 5, 5, 3, 3, 2, 2, 1, 0]; violations: 0
   (the broom with its spine realised attains N-k for every k: its A_k is every input outside v_1..v_{k-1})
   n=2: broom attains |A_k| = N-k for all k: True
   n=3: broom attains |A_k| = N-k for all k: True
   n=4: broom attains |A_k| = N-k for all k: True

