   (at k = N/3 the broom is expensive in this prior and the cyclic route wins; at k = N/2 = 2^(n-1) the broom
    route costs 2 + log2(n(n-1)) bits against n for the cyclic route, so it wins from n = 8 on (by 3.0 bits at
    n = 12). SFI has K(N/2) <= K(n) + c, so for SFI the old e3 proxy, which has no broom, overstates the
    k = N/2 cost by n - O(log n) bits)

